    <string name="settings_privacy_subtitle">What Focuno reads, and never does</string>
    <string name="privacy_title">Privacy</string>
    <string name="privacy_paragraph">Focuno works entirely on your phone. It has no accounts, no analytics and no internet permission, so nothing about you can leave this device. Your usage history lives in a private database on this phone and is deleted when you uninstall.</string>
    <string name="privacy_reads_title">What it reads</string>
    <string name="privacy_reads_body">Which app is in front of you, and how long each app is used. If you choose to block only Reels or Shorts, Focuno also checks a few technical screen-part names inside Instagram or YouTube to see whether the video screen is open. That check only happens while such a rule exists and one of those apps is open.</string>
    <string name="privacy_never_title">What it never touches</string>
    <string name="privacy_never_body">Messages, photos, passwords, text on screen, usernames, captions, your location, contacts, or anything you type in other apps. The only text Focuno keeps is what you type into Focuno itself: unlock reasons, subject names and your exam name. It stays on this phone, and leaves it only if you export it to a file you choose.</string>

